  "outcome": "escalate",
  "rationale": "We are escalating this claim to a senior adjuster because the claimant's statement reveals that the damage includes panels that had been rusting and cracking from age for years, raising uncertainty about whether the claimed damages qualify as a direct and accidental loss. This decision is governed by the collision coverage clause which requires the loss to be accidental. The key fact is that the claimant admitted parts of the damage stem from long-term deterioration rather than the collision itself.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "clause_id": "BASIC-2.1",
      "quote": "direct and accidental loss to the covered vehicle caused by collision"
    }
  ]
}
